# Frontend and UI rules

- Reuse design tokens (`packages/design-tokens`), existing components, and visual system from ADR-004 before inventing new patterns.
- Implement loading, empty, error, success, disabled, and permission-denied states where applicable.
- Build responsive behavior intentionally; do not only optimize for one viewport.
- Preserve keyboard navigation, visible focus, semantic HTML, labels, accessible names, and sensible reading order.
- Do not encode essential meaning using color alone.
- Keep server data, local UI state, form state, and URL state separate.
- Avoid unnecessary client-side rendering, effects, re-renders, and large dependencies.
- Use image/asset pipelines already in-repo (`next/image`, content-icon/WebP scripts); do not embed external assets without permission.
- Validate forms on both client and server boundaries.
- Verify significant UI changes in a real browser for critical flows; gates: `pnpm lint:web`, `pnpm test:web`, and `pnpm build:web` when user-facing.
- Widget changes: build in `packages/support-chat-widget` (npm), then refresh `apps/web/public/chat/og-chat.js` via `chat:build` when embedding.
